#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# log2

#% text
# `log2(x)` gives the base-2 logarithm of `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# An exact power of 2 gives its exponent; any other argument becomes `log(x)/log(2)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
log2(2^5)
#% output
#= 5

#% cell
log2(1/2)
#% output
#= -1

#% cell
log2(x)
#% output
#= log(x)/log(2)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
log2(3.0)
#% output
#= 1.5849625007211563

#% cell
n(log2(3), 25)
#% output
#= 1.584962500721156181453738944

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `log`, `log_base`, `exp`
